+  // first pictures of a stream may come without it): in an output mode in which native output
+  // is to be had, nothing is sent as HDR10 on the way to it. (In another mode it is: a video
+  // that starts in a window, or with a GUI that is not 3840x2160, is HDR10 until the mode for
+  // native output comes, as the base layer of any other stream is shown until then.)
+  const auto* window =
+      dynamic_cast<KODI::WINDOWING::GBM::CWinSystemGbmGLESContext*>(CServiceBroker::GetWinSystem());
+  return window && !(window->SupportsNativeDVOutput() && CanRenderDVBridge(picture));
